        "S4"
      ],
      "timestamp": "2026-09-25T11:58:46.324064Z",
      "user_text": "With this setup, define the expected total cost $C(Q)=E_D[\\text{overage}+\\text{underage}]$, as a function of the order quantity $Q$, as the sum of the expected overage and underage costs — already integrated over $D$'s uniform density (this is the closed form one gets after evaluating $\\int_a^Q c_o(Q-D)\\frac1{b-a}\\,dD+\\int_Q^b c_u(D-Q)\\frac1{b-a}\\,dD$ by hand), so $D$ does not appear here; only its distribution's parameters $a,b$ do.",
      "visible_action": "Memo",
      "operation": null,
      "operation_args": {},
      "backend": null,
      "rendered_command": null,
      "show_command_to_user": false,
      "input_refs": [],
